            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI'd like to avoid depending on yet another third party (VS Code) standard. Not only due to it being an extra (implicit) dependency, but also languages in that 'package.json' file are not designed to be aligned with Neovim's filetypes or tree-sitter languages. This can lead to a very tricky issues.\n\nHow did you use `from_lang()` generator? There are [several 'javascript' sub-files](https://github.com/rafamadriz/friendly-snippets/tree/main/snippets/javascript) and all of them should be loaded for 'javascript' filetype. If you want something specific for a filetype, you can adjust [`lang_patterns` option](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/4521dffdcc5eaab8afa01635961c8c39428b9fc2/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L782-L794) (here is [an example](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/4521dffdcc5eaab8afa01635961c8c39428b9fc2/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L808-L816)).\n\nDo you mind provide an exact reproduction steps for your case? ('mini.snippets' setup, file name/contents/position at which you don't get what you expect)",
