        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Sorry, I should have been more precise. I was not getting any snippets on files with a `.tsx` extension. `lang` is set to `tsx`. I incorrectly assumed `.jsx` files would set `lang` to `jsx` as well. I can provide reproduction steps if they are still needed.\n\nI completely understand not wanting to add a dependency. However, adding manifest support improves the out of the box experience with snippet collection plugins. It allows access to their global snippets, and it allows for better scoping of snippets (I was getting angular snippets on typescript files).\n\nThe generator I propose should probably be renamed from `from_vscode_extension_manifest`. It's designed around \"rafamadriz/friendly-snippets\", and I don't think it follows the VS Code extension manifest standard. It sets `language` to arrays and does not define global snippets in a file with a `.code-snippets` extension. It also seems to prefer Neovim filetypes over [VS Code language identifiers](https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/languages/identifiers) (e.g. `gitcommit` over `git-commit`), but I assume all plugins in Neovim's 'runtimepath' would do this.",
