            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I use `vim.treesitter.language.get_filetypes` in my implementation for the cases where the filetype does not match the parser name, and it works great. I get snippets for the cursor's context.\n\nI think the setup you suggested would still load angular snippets in `tsx` files and would not load the plugin's global snippets.\n\nThe 'package.json' allows the plugin author to group their snippets together based on language. I believe the misalignments introduced by 'friendly-snippets' make adding support for it much simpler.",
