            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I think the setup you suggested would still load angular snippets in `tsx` files and would not load the plugin's global snippets.\n\nSure, the exact details of which snippet file to load is up to the user. The general design of 'mini.snippets' setup is more oriented towards nudging users to be aware of which and how snippets are loaded.\n\n> The 'package.json' allows the plugin author to group their snippets together based on language. I believe the misalignments introduced by 'friendly-snippets' make adding support for it much simpler.\n\nYet it is still a single plugin and adding built-in support for *its* variant of 'package.json' (which is not entirely concise) is a bit too much for 'mini.snippets' as built-in. It'd be useful as a code snippet to put in user's config (and maybe future wiki), if you'll have something you feel comfortable sharing.",
